= Li Zeng's Research

== Space Computing Power Networks

=== Research Watchlist
==== Projects
- [research-watchlist/orbital-compute.html orbital-compute] (2026) — An open-source simulator for evaluating orbital GPU computing across mechanics, power, thermal, networking, scheduling, and economics. [https://github.com/ShipItAndPray/orbital-compute \[Repository\]] [https://shipitandpray.github.io/orbital-compute/index.html \[Live Demo\]]
- [research-watchlist/leocc.html LeoCC] (2025) — A reconfiguration-aware congestion-control system that remains robust to fast-changing LEO paths. [https://github.com/SpaceNetLab/LeoCC \[Repository\]] [https://doi.org/10.1145/3718958.3750491 \[Paper\]]
- [research-watchlist/leocraft.html LEOCraft] (2025) — A modular flow-level simulator for rapid evaluation of LEO constellation throughput, latency, routing, and coverage. [https://github.com/suvambasak/LEOCraft \[Repository\]] [https://suvambasak.github.io/LEOCraft/ \[Documentation\]] [https://www.usenix.org/conference/atc25/presentation/basak \[Paper\]]
- [research-watchlist/xingkan-satellite-digital-twin.html Xingkan Satellite Digital Twin] (2026) — An interactive digital-twin system for visualizing global satellite constellations using real-time and historical TLE data. [https://xingkan-satellite-digital-twin.onrender.com/ \[Live Demo\]]
- [research-watchlist/paseos.html PASEOS] (2024) — A decentralized Python environment simulator for spacecraft operations under power, thermal, radiation, orbit, and communication constraints. [https://github.com/aidotse/PASEOS \[Repository\]] [https://paseos.readthedocs.io/ \[Documentation\]] [https://doi.org/10.1109/JSTARS.2024.3445506 \[Paper\]]
- [research-watchlist/leoem.html LeoEM] (2023) — A real-time emulator that turns time-varying LEO topology and routes into native Linux network paths for end-to-end experiments. [https://github.com/XuyangCaoUCSD/LeoEM \[Repository\]] [https://doi.org/10.1109/INFOCOM53939.2023.10228914 \[Paper\]]

==== Datasets
- [research-watchlist/satellite-image-deep-learning-datasets.html satellite-image-deep-learning/datasets] (2022) — A living catalog of satellite and aerial imagery datasets for deep learning, organized by sensor, platform, and task. [https://github.com/satellite-image-deep-learning/datasets \[Repository\]]
- [research-watchlist/torchgeo-datasets.html TorchGeo Datasets] (2021) — A maintained collection of geospatial datasets with PyTorch-ready loaders, metadata-aware composition, and benchmark support. [https://github.com/torchgeo/torchgeo \[Repository\]] [https://docs.torchgeo.org/en/stable/api/datasets.html \[Documentation\]] [https://doi.org/10.1145/3707459 \[Paper\]]
- [research-watchlist/mobicom24-satellitecots.html MobiCom24-SatelliteCOTS] (2024) — Real in-orbit telemetry and experiment code for studying the thermal and energy behavior of COTS computing payloads on BUPT-1. [https://github.com/TiansuanConstellation/MobiCom24-SatelliteCOTS \[Repository\]] [https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.03435 \[Paper\]]
- [research-watchlist/lens.html LENS] (2024) — A multi-location, longitudinal Starlink measurement dataset with raw and processed network-performance snapshots. [https://github.com/clarkzjw/LENS \[Repository\]] [https://lens-starlink.jinwei.me/ \[Dataset Portal\]] [https://doi.org/10.1145/3625468.3652170 \[Paper\]]
- [research-watchlist/wetlinks.html WetLinks] (2024) — A longitudinal Starlink dataset that aligns throughput, latency, routing, terminal telemetry, and contiguous weather observations. [https://github.com/sys-uos/WetLinks \[Repository\]] [https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.16448 \[Paper\]]
- [research-watchlist/esa-anomaly-dataset.html ESA Anomalies Dataset & ESA-ADB] (2024) — A three-mission satellite-telemetry dataset with curated anomaly annotations and a reproducible evaluation benchmark. [https://esoc.esa.int/esa-releases-building-block-open-database-satellite-anomalies \[Official Page\]] [https://github.com/esa/anomaly-dataset \[Repository\]] [https://zenodo.org/records/12528696 \[Data\]] [https://github.com/kplabs-pl/ESA-ADB \[Benchmark\]] [https://openreview.net/forum?id=bbpRMoatVO \[Paper\]] [https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.17826 \[Preprint\]]
- [research-watchlist/opssat-ad.html OPSSAT-AD] (2024) — An AI-ready anomaly-detection benchmark built from annotated telemetry segments collected aboard ESA's OPS-SAT CubeSat. [https://github.com/kplabs-pl/OPS-SAT-AD \[Repository\]] [https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.12588358 \[Data\]] [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-025-05035-3 \[Paper\]] [https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.04730 \[Preprint\]]

